  "entry": "code/server.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Takes a mature miRNA sequence and builds candidate forward and reverse qPCR primers using the miR-specific qPCR rules of Balcells, Cirera & Busk 2011 (BMC Biotechnology 11:70), listing each primer's sequence, length, Tm and three pass/fail flags for A/T content at the 3' end. The reverse primers carry a poly-T stretch, so they are meant for poly(A)-tailed cDNA. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
